      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Of course, we can definitely highlight their otherworldly appearance to encapsulate their untamed essence. The Draknor people stand around 6 feet tall, though their preternatural agility and muscular physique often give them an uncanny, almost skeletal look. Their skin is a camouflaged maroon-brown, perfectly blending with the thick mosses and stones of their surrounds, making them nearly invisible in the wild.\n\nIn crowded gatherings, the Draknor appear wild and primal, with their movements organic and instinct-driven. They do not observe formal seating arrangements; instead, they radiate a multitudes of energy when riled, with soft growls vibrating through their clenched teeth and flickering eyes that are a deep crimson even in the faintest light. Many of their community members wear unconventional garb—cloaked in leather-like hides, decorated with earthy pigments and worn bones, exuding an uncomfortable, almost savage aura.\n\nTheir unruly disarray reflects their inclination towards instinct over reason, defying the meticulousness of the empire’s civilians. Rather painfully, one around them might feel their unyielding drive, dangerously reminiscent of untamed beasts in complete disregard of convention. Their presence in a crowd would feel like a primal challenge to",
